     rrrreennuummdd — router renumbering daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     rrrreennuummdd [--ddff] [--cc _c_o_n_f___f_i_l_e | --ss]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrrreennuummdd utility transmits router renumbering request packets, to
     renumber the routers in the site network.

     On KAME-based systems, router renumbering requests are received and pro‐
     cessed by rtadvd(8).  For other systems, refer to relevant documents.

     The program will daemonize itself on invocation.  It reads configuration
     information from standard input if --ss is specified, or from _c_o_n_f___f_i_l_e if
     --cc _c_o_n_f___f_i_l_e is specified.

     The contents of configuration information are described in
     rrenumd.conf(5).

     After successful configuration, rrrreennuummdd sends router renumbering messages
     periodically to configured destinations.  Messages contain prefixes con‐
     figured to be renumbered.

     --dd      Debug mode.

     --ff      Foreground mode.  Do not become daemon.

     --ss      Script mode.  Configuration information is obtained from standard
             input.

     --cc _c_o_n_f___f_i_l_e
             Specify a configuration file where configuration information is
             kept.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The program exits with 0 on success, and non-zero on failures.

